+## Loom step-limit pauses
+
+A Loom run paused with `step_limit` remains attached to its conversation. ZiNuSya
+sends one notice per observed pause through the durable outbox with Continue and Stop reply
+buttons instead of presenting a retained question or approval. Repeated polls and bot
+restarts do not resend that notice. A later message accepted into the same paused
+run receives its own notice unless the input receipt says Loom has left the pause.
+If an input already committed a notice for the observed version, the parent
+adopts that presentation instead of sending another copy.
+The notice asks whether to continue or stop and explains that prior actions are
+not undone. Both buttons send ordinary conversation text, like a typed reply;
+Loom owns processing that choice and renewing the step budget. The buttons do not
+claim that the queued message was processed or that the run has already resumed.
+Delivery compares the active run with newer input receipts from the same run.
+Unrelated menus preserve the pause choices; delayed notices cannot restore them
+after the run has moved on. Completion also retires choices delivered by an input
+task before the parent worker observed the pause.
+
+ZiNuSya does not resume or replace this run, reset its budget, or replay its actions.
+Polling continues so Loom can resume the original run and deliver its eventual result.
+
